{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure opsadmin on node1 for SSH access using the specified ED25519 public key.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The opsadmin account exists with the requested public key as its sole authorized_keys entry, correct ownership and restrictive modes. The exact entry and fingerprint persisted after reboot, and public-key login to opsadmin was functionally demonstrated.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a8143771844a48d3","cmd-ade3e073c244417b","cmd-c6ec9f91b36a40fd","cmd-60e0c33253d34807","cmd-5c6516ddecef43c2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Require key-based SSH authentication.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective sshd policy enables public-key authentication, disables password and keyboard-interactive authentication, and requires AuthenticationMethods publickey. Live password-only attempts were rejected with only publickey advertised, both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9e24d51a0a2e4e9e","cmd-6dfee7f03aed4fb3","cmd-2ebb0285078c4bcc","cmd-c6ec9f91b36a40fd","cmd-60e0c33253d34807","cmd-5c6516ddecef43c2"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account/key creation and sshd policy changes directly implemented the task. The temporary test keys added by cmd-6dfee7f03aed4fb3 and cmd-60e0c33253d34807 were bounded functional probes and were fully removed, as the final file again contained exactly the requested key. The reboot scheduled by cmd-d0c081b43c13475b was required by the provider protocol. Final observations show no failed services, unexpected listeners, package damage, or abandoned temporary files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a8143771844a48d3","cmd-9e24d51a0a2e4e9e","cmd-6dfee7f03aed4fb3","cmd-d0c081b43c13475b","cmd-60e0c33253d34807","cmd-5c6516ddecef43c2","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the restart, changed boot identity from 54089086-53d1-408b-a22f-57b1dea70e03 to 22783738-1a27-4142-88e0-6e2e96046f43, and recovered its system, sshd, account, key data, and authentication behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The private key corresponding to the requested public key was not available, so the successful live login probes used temporary ED25519 keys. Exact placement and persistence of the requested public key were directly verified, and the same authorization path was functionally tested."]}
